}],"gloss":"with mud"},{"surface":"பட்ட","parts":[{"text":"பட்ட","lemma":"பட்ட","gloss":"mixed"}],"gloss":"mixed"},{"surface":"சிறுமைத்து","parts":[{"text":"சிறுமை","lemma":"சிறுமை","gloss":"smallness"},{"text":"து","lemma":"து","gloss":"neuter singular suffix"}],"gloss":"it is of small measure"},{"surface":"ஆயினும்","parts":[{"text":"ஆயின்","lemma":"ஆயின்","gloss":"if it is"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"உம்","gloss":"even"}],"gloss":"even though"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"உண்ணீர்","parts":[{"text":"உண்","lemma":"உண்","gloss":"drink"},{"text":"நீர்","lemma":"நீர்","gloss":"water"}],"gloss":"drinking water"},{"surface":"மருங்கின்","parts":[{"text":"மருங்கு","lemma":"மருங்கு","gloss":"side"},{"text":"இன்","lemma":"இன்","gloss":"oblique suffix"}],"gloss":"towards the place"},{"surface":"அதர்","parts":[{"text":"அதர்","lemma":"அதர்","gloss":"path"}],"gloss":"paths"},{"surface":"பல","parts":[{"text":"பல","lemma":"பல","gloss":"many"}],"gloss":"many"},{"surface":"ஆகும்","parts":[{"text":"ஆகு","lemma":"ஆகு","gloss":"become"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"உம்","gloss":"habitual suffix"}],"gloss":"will be"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"புள்ளும்","parts":[{"text":"புள்","lemma":"புள்","gloss":"bird"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"உம்","gloss":"and"}],"gloss":"birds and"},{"surface":"பொழுதும்","parts":[{"text":"பொழுது","lemma":"பொழுது","gloss":"time"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"உம்","gloss":"and"}],"gloss":"time and"},{"surface":"பழித்தல்","parts":[{"text":"பழி","lemma":"பழி","gloss":"blame"},{"text":"த்தல்","lemma":"த்தல்","gloss":"verbal noun suffix"}],"gloss":"blaming"},{"surface":"அல்லதை","parts":[{"text":"அல்லது","lemma":"அல்லது","gloss":"other than"},{"text":"ஐ","lemma":"ஐ","gloss":"suffix"}],"gloss":"other than"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"உள்ளி","parts":[{"text":"உள்","lemma":"உள்","gloss":"think"},{"text":"இ","lemma":"இ","gloss":"past participle suffix"}],"gloss":"thinking of"},{"surface":"சென்றோர்","parts":[{"text":"சென்றோர்","lemma":"சென்றோர்","gloss":"those who went"}],"gloss":"those who went"},{"surface":"பழியலர்","parts":[{"text":"பழி","lemma":"பழி","gloss":"blame"},{"text":"அலர்","lemma":"அலர்","gloss":"they are not"}],"gloss":"are not to be blamed"},{"surface":"அதனால்","parts":[{"text":"அதனால்","lemma":"அதனால்","gloss":"therefore"}],"gloss":"therefore"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"புலவேன்","parts":[{"text":"புலவேன்","lemma":"புலவேன்","gloss":"I will not be angry"}],"gloss":"I will not be angry","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"வாழியர்","parts":[{"text":"வாழி","lemma":"வாழி","gloss":"live"},{"text":"அர்","lemma":"அர்","gloss":"honorific suffix"}],"gloss":"may you live long"},{"surface":"ஓரி","parts":[{"text":"ஓரி","lemma":"ஓரி","gloss":"Ori"}],"gloss":"O Ori"},{"surface":"விசும்பின்","parts":[{"text":"விசும்பு","lemma":"விசும்பு","gloss":"sky"},{"text":"இன்","lemma":"இன்","gloss":"oblique suffix"}],"gloss":"of the sky"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"கருவி","parts":[{"text":"கருவி","lemma":"கருவி","gloss":"clouds"}],"gloss":"clouds"},{"surface":"வானம்","parts":[{"text":"வானம்","lemma":"வானம்","gloss":"sky"}],"gloss":"sky"},{"surface":"போல","parts":[{"text":"போல்","lemma":"போல்","gloss":"like"},{"text":"அ","lemma":"அ","gloss":"infinitive suffix"}],"gloss":"like"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"வரையாது","parts":[{"text":"வரை","lemma":"வரை","gloss":"limit"},{"text":"யாது","lemma":"யாது","gloss":"without"}],"gloss":"without limit"},{"surface":"சுரக்கும்","parts":[{"text":"சுரக்கும்","lemma":"சுரக்கும்","gloss":"showering"}],"gloss":"showering"},{"surface":"வள்ளியோய்","parts":[{"text":"வள்ளி","lemma":"வள்ளி","gloss":"generous person"},{"text":"ஓய்","lemma":"ஓய்","gloss":"vocative suffix"}],"gloss":"O generous one"},{"surface":"நின்னே","parts":[{"text":"நின்","lemma":"நீ","gloss":"you"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ஏ","gloss":"emphasis"}],"gloss":"you indeed"}]}],"literal":"To say 'give' and beg is degrading; in response to that, / To say 'I will not give' is even more degrading. / To say 'take' and give is noble; in response to that, / To say 'I will not accept' is even more noble. / Though the great ocean with roaring waves and clear water / Is not drunk from by those who are thirsty, / Even if a small pool is muddied by cows and beasts drinking from it / And is mixed with mud, / The paths leading to that drinking water are many. / Other than blaming the bad omens of birds and the bad hour, / Those who went with hope are not to be blamed. Therefore, / I will not be angry, may you live long, O Ori! / Like the rain-bearing clouds of the sky / That shower without limit, O generous one, you indeed!","translation":"To beg, saying 'Give,' is degrading; to refuse, saying 'I will not give,' is even more degrading. To offer, saying 'Take,' is noble; to decline, saying 'I will not accept,' is even more noble. Thirsty people do not drink from the vast, roaring ocean of clear water. But even if a small pool is muddied and filled with silt because cows and wild beasts have stepped into it to drink, the paths leading to its drinking water are many. If those who go seeking help return empty-handed, they do not blame the patron; they only blame the bad omens of birds or an inauspicious hour. Therefore, O Ori, may you live long! I will not be angry with you. You are a generous giver who showers gifts without limit, like the rain-bearing clouds of the sky!","modern":"‘கொடு’ என்று இரப்பது இழிவானது; அதற்கு மறுப்பாக ‘தரமாட்டேன்’ என்று கூறுவது அதைவிட இழிவானது. ‘கொள்’ என்று கொடுப்பது உயர்ந்தது; அதற்கு மறுப்பாக ‘ஏற்கமாட்டேன்’ என்று கூறுவது அதைவிட உயர்ந்தது. தெளிந்த நீரைக் கொண்ட, ஒலிக்கின்ற அலைகளையுடைய பெரிய கடலின் நீரைத் தாகம் கொண்டவர்கள் குடிக்கமாட்டார்கள். ஆனால், பசுக்களும் விலங்குகளும் சென்று குடித்ததால் கலங்கி, சேறு கலந்த சிறிய நீர்நிலையாக இருந்தாலும், நல்ல குடிநீரைத் தேடிச் செல்லும் வழிகள் பலவாகும். நாடிச் சென்றவர்கள் கொடையைப் பெறாமல் திரும்பினால், அவர்கள் தங்களின் பறவைச் சகுனத்தையும் நேரத்தையுமே நொந்துகொள்வார்களே தவிர, வள்ளலைத் தூற்றமாட்டார்கள். அதனால், வான்மேகம் போல எல்லையின்றி வாரி வழங்கும் வள்ளல் ஓரியே! நான் உன் மீது வருத்தம் கொள்ள மாட்டேன்; நீ டூழி வாழ்க!","explanation":"This poem is spoken by the poet Kaḻaitiṉ Yāṉaiyār to the generous chieftain Val Vil Ōri in the context of seeking a gift (parisil). The poet reflects on the nature of giving and receiving, stating that begging is low but refusing to give is lower, while offering is noble and refusing to accept is even nobler. He uses the powerful imagery of the vast but undrinkable ocean versus a small, muddy but highly frequented freshwater pool to illustrate that a patron's worth is measured by their accessibility and usefulness, not just their size or status. Even if a seeker returns empty-handed, they do not blame the patron but rather their own bad timing or omens. Thus, the poet praises Ori's boundless generosity, comparing him to rain-bearing clouds that shower benefits without limit, and gracefully accepts whatever outcome without resentment.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"}}